.kilo

# Go template downloaded with gut

### Go ###
# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Extensionless Linux binaries (e.g. `go build ./cmd/solvent`)
#
# These have to be enumerated by name: they have no extension to match on, and a
# blanket rule would ignore real files. This list was short by three, and the three
# it missed got committed — 45 MB of unstripped ELF with debug info, 91.7% of every
# tracked byte in the repository, referenced by nothing. The Dockerfile rebuilds from
# source into different names, so they were pure weight.
#
# `operator-review` in particular is rebuilt into the repo root by
# scripts/demo/setup.sh on every `task setup`, which is how it kept coming back.
/solvent
/solvent-mcp
/web
/init
/operator-review
/bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

.gut

# Phase 3 corpus snapshot — fetched GitHub data, never committed.
# The canonical snapshot lives here (NDJSON + .meta.json) and is the artifact
# both local and cloud ingestion consume. It is reproducible via
# `task corpus:fetch`, so there is no reason to track it.
/corpus-data/
*.ndjson
